<title>BELGIUM: EP approves appointment of Duisenberg to head EMI.</title>
<headline>EP approves appointment of Duisenberg to head EMI.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament endorsed on Thursday the appointment of Wim Duisenberg as president of the European Monetary Institute, the forerunner of the European Central Bank (ECB).</p>
<p>Duisenberg, who is currently the governor of the Dutch central bank, has expressed an interest in running the ECB.</p>
<p>He will take over from Alexander Lamfalussy as head of the EMI on July 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Euro-MPs agreed Lamfalussy's mandate, which should have ended on January 1, 1997, should be extended for six months until 30 June 1997.</p>
</text>
